 {"id":"OB-OPS-008","title":"[done] Corpus catch-up export + hygiene repair: sanctioned export replaces 3 hand-written files, +2574 answers","status":"complete","priority":"P2","complexity":1,"capability_tags":["corpus","data-hygiene","distribution"],"created_at":"2026-11-21T03:24:16Z","updated_at":"2026-11-21T03:24:16Z","completed_at":"2026-11-21T03:24:16Z","depends_on":[],"blocks":[],"reasoning":"WHY: three corpus files (3329-3331) had been hand-written ~9h before this tick and FAILED the repo's own make check-corpus-hygiene (absolute /home/<user> paths, bare IPv4 literal) because they bypassed scripts/export-answers.py, the only path that normalizes home->~ and redacts IPs. Separately the live DB held a backfill of 2574 verified answers that the corpus had never carried (corpus ~30 classes/day behind; the 05:00 ob1-distribute cron had not yet run). WHAT: ran the sanctioned exporter against off-by-one.db. It removed the 3 hand-written files, re-emitted the same 3 classes as sanitized ids 3336-3338, and caught the rest of the DB up. Note answer_id collisions (5063-5065) with committed 3326-3328 are harmless: internal/seed/seed.go dedupes on content identity and ignores answer_id (export-scoped).","worker_status":"foreman-inline","worker_summary":"Mechanical data work performed by the foreman with the repo's own sanctioned script; no worker dispatched because there was no dispatchable board row and this is data generation, not code authoring.","commit_hash":"d3d85a354197446e89536734c776892555d31f06","files_changed":2255,"lines_added":54135,"lines_removed":2247,"guard_result":"Tier 1 DEGRADED PASS (no Go source staged; secrets clean)","ci_result":"success (both runs on d7837da9: main workflow + pages build and deployment)","review_notes":"Corpus export commit = d7837da9 (2255 files, +54135/-2247). This row lives in the board commit d3d85a35 because the gitreins closeout gate requires row.commit_hash to equal the tree it grades; the corpus work itself is verified at d