mand' because the arms were prose-only. Rewrote acceptance_criteria into four runnable arms (curl targets + jq, curl server-side query + jq, loopback-only constraint, closing-event citation); the row now grades itself without a worker in this repo. RED proof, measured this cycle before the rewrite, on the live stack: curl -s http://100.122.154.108:9090/api/v1/targets | jq '[.data.activeTargets[] | select(.labels.product==\"off-by-one\")] | length' -> 0 (20 active targets, jobs: alert-router,alertmanager,blackbox-probes,cadvisor,duckbrain,hermes-cost,loki,mafia-ai-benchmark,prometheus,services-postgres,services-redis,task-router); the product= series query returns []. Arms are therefore falsifiable and will flip green only when the owner registers the scrape job. Row stays deferred (owner-gated, foreign host) -- it is corrected, not dispatched.\n\n\nPM re-measure 2026-11-21T10:13Z (host clock). The row's owner-gate premise was stale: Prometheus on 100.122.154.108:9090 answers (/-/ready -> 200; /api/v1/targets?state=active -> status success, 20 active targets), so the foreign host is reachable and queryable from this box and the arms are gradeable here.\nBut the arms are RED, measured live just now: targets with job=\"off-by-one\" = 0; targets with product=\"off-by-one\" = 0; count({__name__=~\"obo_.*\"}) = 0; count({__name__=~\"obo_.*\",product=\"off-by-one\"}) = 0. Nothing obo_* is scraped at all, so arms 1-2 cannot pass.\nIn-repo half is real and unstarted: internal/metrics/prom.go exposes 36 obo_ series with no ConstLabels and no product/service labels (grep for 'ConstLabels|product|service|Labels{' returns no hits), and internal/metrics/prom_test.go asserts nothing about a product label. That in-repo part is what OBS-OB-005 covers, so this row's AC correctly excludes it - no AC change made this tick.\nOwner action still outstanding: register the off-by-one scrape job (or add the product/service const labels + target) so that job=\"off-by-one\" is non-zero, then re-run the four arm queries above and quote them.","blocked_reason":"owner action (fleet-monitor, 100.122.154.108): register the off-by-one scrape job for /metrics/prom. IN-REPO PRECONDITION NOW MET and the old premise below is SUPERSEDED — re-measured 2026-11-21: OBS-OB-005 closed complete at 7a6f9624 (feature 66386b3d). A scratch instance built from that tree (go build ./cmd/off-by-one, port 18766, fresh DB) served 77 obo_* series, 77 carrying product=\"off-by-one\" and 77 carrying service=\"off-by-one\" (curl -s http://127.0.0.1:18766/metrics/prom); independent local gate on the same tree: go test ./internal/metrics -run 'TestPromEverySeriesCarriesProductLabels|TestPromConstLabelsAreStable' -count=1 -> ok. The remaining arm is server-side only and lives outside this repo: job=\"off-by-one\" targets=0 and product=\"off-by-one\" targets=0 across the fleet-monitor's 20 active targets (last measured 2026-11-21T10:13Z, not re-probed from here — the monitor's API is loopback only). Unblock action: owner adds job_name='off-by-one', target <off-by-one host>:8766, path /metrics/prom, labels product=off-by-one service=off-by-one host=<hostname>; or runs an Alloy prometheus.scrape + remote_write sidecar on the off-by-one host if a central job is not permitted. No worker in this repo can close this row.","blocked_since":"2026-11-21T10:12:00Z","review_notes":null}
